      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Method",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Toss the daikon and carrot matchsticks with a pinch of seasoning. Squeeze gently and leave for 10 minutes to soften. Rinse and drain well.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Mix 2 tbsp sugar with the lime juice and 2 tbsp of water. Pour over the drained vegetables. Leave to pickle for at least 1 hour.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Mix the fish sauce, soy sauce, 1 tbsp sugar, and garlic in a bowl. Add the sliced pork and toss to coat. Marinate for at least 20 minutes.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Heat the vegetable oil in a frying pan over high heat. Cook the pork in a single layer for 2 to 3 minutes per side until caramelised and cooked through. Work in batches if needed.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Slice the baguettes lengthways, cutting almost but not all the way through. Open them out and place under a hot grill for 2 minutes until the inside is lightly toasted.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Layer the pork slices along the bottom half of each baguette.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Drain the pickled vegetables well and pile them on top of the pork. Add the cucumber strips, fresh coriander, and sliced chilli.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Drizzle with a little extra fish sauce if you like. Close the sandwich and serve straight away.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          }
        ],
        "type": "orderedList"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Rinse after 10 minutes and do not over-soak. One to two hours in the brine is plenty.",
              "cause": "They were left in the salt or brine for too long.",
              "symptom": "The pickled vegetables are too soft and mushy."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Slice pork as thin as possible. Cook on the highest heat in small batches so the pan stays very hot.",
              "cause": "The slices were too thick or the pan was not hot enough.",
              "symptom": "The pork is tough and chewy."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Drain the pickled vegetables thoroughly before adding. Assemble and eat straight away.",
              "cause": "Wet fillings were added without draining properly.",
              "symptom": "The bread goes soggy quickly."
            }
          }
        ],
        "type": "troubleshooter"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Where this dish lives",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Bánh mì comes from the French colonial period in Vietnam. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Vietnamese bakers made the baguette lighter and shorter to suit local tastes. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Street stalls selling bánh mì became common across the country from the mid-20th century. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Southern versions often include pâté and cold cuts alongside grilled meat. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Today it is sold on almost every street in Ho Chi Minh City and has spread worldwide.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      }
    ],
    "type": "doc"
  },
